WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.490
Island!
An island is in sight!

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.460
Yes, it's an island!
An island! An island!

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.450
Really, an island?
An island!

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.170
Say, Mr. Trelawney, could that be...
Is that our island?

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.810
Tell me it is!

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.120
Don't get all excited.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.770
That isn't it, Jim. That's not
the island we're searching for.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.190
Aw man, seriously?

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.730
However...!
It's still an island!

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.150
It's been so long!

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.130
<i>We left Bristol a month ago.</i>

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.730
<i>After all those days at sea, the Hispaniola docked...</i>

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.730
<i>...at a small city port in the West Indies.</i>

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.000
<i>It was so nice to see land again.</i>

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.950
Treasure
Island

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.750
Takarajima

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.560
saa ikou

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.560
Come, let's go

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.650
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.650
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.490
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.490
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.370
umi hedeyou

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.370
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.290
ikute ni wa

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.290
Many of us

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.290
minna mada shiranai

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.290
Still don't know of

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.040
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.040
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.540
matte iru darou

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.540
That await us there

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.050
itsumo shinji you

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.050
We must always have trust

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.300
magokoro wo

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.300
And be sincere

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:56.560
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:56.560
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.690
tade hitotsu no

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.690
I only...

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.110
akogare dake wa

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.110
...have one desire

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.400
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.400
And no one...

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:12.110
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:12.110
...will ever take it away

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.660
tade hitotsu no

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.660
I only...

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.960
akogare dake wa

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.960
...have one desire

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.290
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.290
And no one...

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:31.220
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:31.220
...will ever take it away

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.600
episode

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.600
Kidnapping
\h     in the Slave Port

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.310
We'll resupply food and water in this port.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.620
We will also repair the damage caused by the storm.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.900
Aye, Captain!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.240
Master Cook Silver.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.220
Take three men to buy food.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.450
Aye-aye, sir.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.020
Very well!
The others will remain on board...

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.410
...to finish the repairs by
the end of the afternoon.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.870
Captain, don't do this.
We want to go on land.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.860
We'll cast off at 7pm!
That is all!

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.290
No more questions.
Get to work.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.680
Silver, dirty traitor!
Why didn't you pick me?!

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.140
That's the way it is, Anderson.
The number of places is limited.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.100
Bastard! I hope that your stomach bursts when you stuff yourself!

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.880
That's my intention!
I assure you!

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.070
<i>Of course I was one of those chosen to bring back food.</i>

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.990
<i>Silver knew that I wanted to go.</i>

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.580
Butcher, show me your pork and beef.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.980
Alright.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.940
My men are picky, I want good quality.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.770
Right, I understand.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:14.690
What do you think of this?
It's of the finest quality.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.910
"Finest quality"?
Stop pulling my leg.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.150
There's more water than meat.
Anyone could tell.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.780
There's no fooling you, dear customer.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.110
You have a keen eye.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.830
Naturally. I've been in the business for 25 years.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.920
Hey, Jim.
Stay in front of us.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.880
Don't worry!
I can take care of myself.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.780
Say, Silver.
What do you call these flowers?

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.930
Hibiscus.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.860
Silver...

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.950
They're slaves. They're captured in Africa to be sold.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.940
Watch out, Jim. Besides Blacks,
they also kidnap children your age to sell.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:16.870
R-Really?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.920
Look at that, we're gonna get a shower.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.300
A shower?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.260
It's a squall.
A storm isn't far off.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.640
A storm?

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.200
Silver!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.140
Excuse me, can you help me?

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:12.260
If you please! Did you happen to see three English sailors?

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.480
This is bad.
I'm in big trouble.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.150
Where did they go?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.400
Kid, you looking for someone?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.660
If ya want, we can help you look.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.360
Yeah.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.120
You're English? Thank God,
you understand what I say.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.380
You said it, kid.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.500
Being a foreigner that doesn't speak the language isn't very convenient.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.260
How careless.
Come, we'll lend you a hand.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.100
Come here!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.100
Shut up!

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.400
Hey, Silver!

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.940
He probably took a rowboat back to the ship.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.360
I doubt that. He would've taken this boat if he returned.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.370
Forget him, we have to hurry!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.200
The Hispaniola will depart at sunset!

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.660
Don't be in such a hurry.
We can wait a little longer.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.380
The Captain isn't a patient man.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.410
He'll leave without us.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.370
Hey, Silver!

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.600
What happened, Benbow?
Are you hurt?

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:35.660
What's wrong, boy?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.280
I bet something happened to Jim.
Didn't it?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.310
Silver, leave him!
The sun is—

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.110
Shut up!
If you want to go back, go ahead!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.660
You better stay put until the buyer arrives.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.070
Go on.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:53.930
'Kay.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:02.210
An English child fetches a high price on the market.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.010
That's what happened...

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:20.770
We told him he had to return at the departure time.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.610
You did what you had to.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>In an hour it will be 7pm...</i>

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:30.510
We'll raise anchor in an hour.
Everyone must be ready for the departure!

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.200
Captain, what a minute.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.160
Yes, wait.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.740
You're not going to abandon Jim and Silver, Captain?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:44.120
Captain Smollett, even if they are at fault,
you must reconsider your decision.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:47.130
We raise anchor at 7pm.
We'll stay one hour.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.250
<i>Jim...</i>

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.270
I've gotta pee!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.180
Gotta pee! Pee! Pee!

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.460
Hurry, the rope! The rope! Untie it! Pee! Pee! Pee!

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:10.920
Hold it in!

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:12.820
Did you pee your pants?

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.240
Almost...

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.310
You're impossible.
This way!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.240
Go on, make it quick.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.420
Kid!
Kid, wait!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.380
I really don't have the time!
The ship raises anchor at 7pm!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.380
Where are you going, kid?

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.890
I've just found a generous buyer.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.160
Be a good lad and obey.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.730
Never!

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.870
Wait!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.180
Get your dirty hands off me!

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.250
Let go of him.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.710
Silver!

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:13.410
What are you doing, Jim?
I've looked for you everywhere.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.580
Really, I've always gotta look after you.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.760
So?
Who are these guys?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.430
They're a bunch of kidnappers, Silver!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.690
Bastard!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:33.150
Kidnappers, you say?
That's a frightening job.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.490
It's best not to mess with these guys.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.200
Come on, we're going, Jim.
The others must be worried.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.870
Jim!

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.080
You're asking for it!

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.230
For Pete's sake, all this tells me nothing.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.170
What is it that Jim and Silver are doing?

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.740
Not good, not good...

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.900
Not good at all.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:22.320
Captain, he must have had to get something.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.600
If that wasn't the case, the brave Silver would already be back.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.080
Whatever the reason, we raise the anchor at 7pm. Everyone had been warned.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.190
What did you say?
That's in 5 minutes!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:41.160
Come Captain, I agree that your severity admirably suits your position.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.140
I respect you, truly!

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:47.230
But the difference between Silver and Jim is that Jim is only a child.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:51.560
His mother entrusted him to me.
I am responsible for him!

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.230
Who has a watch on this ship?

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:01.760
Probably only you, Dr. Livesey and myself.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.020
I've had mine a very long time.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.310
Sometimes it's slow.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.660
What about yours?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.630
Mine is new, it's hardly ever slow.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:21.300
Really? Mine likes to be slow by an hour or two.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.430
Hm, what's this?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.350
It even seems to have stopped?

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.220
Mr. Smollett!

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.080
Jim, now!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.090
Okay!

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.090
Damn you...

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.640
Silver, were you hit?!

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.600
Don't worry, it's just a graze.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:22.000
I don't know who's boat this is, but we don't have a choice.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.100
The Hispaniola!

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.420
They waited for us!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:45.840
We're saved!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.490
Really?
That's great, Jim.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.000
Silver!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.700
Silver!

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.590
Silver! Silver!

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:02.610
Silver! Silver! Silver! Silver!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.530
Silver! Silver!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.210
The bullet didn't hit any vital organs.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.620
His life isn't in any danger.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:18.290
But,

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.590
I have to extract the bullet without damage.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.490
Come on, Jim!
Bring back the light!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.070
You're really tough.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:52.290
You've endured everything
without even losing conscience.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.450
This isn't my cabin.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.570
It must be Jim's then.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:34.740
Silver... Silver... Silver...

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.460
That you, Jim?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.820
Yes, sir.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:47.590
You can come in.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:49.040
Pardon me.

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.550
You wanted to see me, Captain?

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:56.940
For whatever reason,
you were late for the departure.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.780
On top of that, Silver has been wounded.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.520
And all of it is your fault.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:02.480
Yes, sir.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.940
I am obligated to punish you.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.900
I am ready, Captain.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:14.360
Consequently, Jim Hawkins, here is
the breakdown of your punishment:

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:19.340
"First. You will be on
potato duty for a week."

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.330
Aye.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.700
"Next. Until Silver has completely recovered,

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:26.460
you will watch over him
and change his bandages."

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.290
That is all.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.710
Aye-aye, sir!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:44.020
Hey, Jim. You'd be better off in the kitchen or on deck.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:48.930
I can't. Don't forget that I have to watch over you too.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.410
You must rest!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.450
Sorry.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.870
A ship!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.940
The Union Jack!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.990
It's a British ship!

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:17.260
But that's...

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.220
A p-p-pirate ship!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.830
Everyone to their post!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.780
Prepare for battle!

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.050
We're in for it now!

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.050
Hurry!

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.060
Silver!
Don't you worry!

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.420
We'll get rid of these pirates in no time!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.380
Sleep soundly.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.380
"Sleep soundly"?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.890
You hear that, Flint?

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.350
We must change direction!
Helm to port!

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.500
Take aim!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.790
Hold your horses!
Don't fire!

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:16.450
Silver!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.410
Silver, what is it?
Why'd you stop them?

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:23.370
Captain, you have the intention of confronting these pirates?

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:24.900
Of course!

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:28.330
Otherwise, I am no longer worthy
to be a subject of King George.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:30.740
That's a remarkable attitude,

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:32.420
but many men will die because of it.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.060
On both sides, that is.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.260
Is that what you want?

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:36.840
What?

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.620
If you let me take the situation into my hands,

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.410
I will rid us of these pirates without trouble.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:46.020
What did you say?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.740
Interesting. Let us see what the Master Cook can do.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.280
Hey, Hands!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.250
Yes?

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:08.210
Helm to starboard!
Course to South!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.330
Aye-aye, sir!

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:20.930
Silver!

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:24.100
Silver, if you're going to flee, I have no need of you.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.700
Don't worry.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.560
It will not dirty the name of our good King George.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.520
Anderson!
Where is the bosun Anderson?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:33.860
Here!

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.480
Go to the powder storeroom and bring three barrels of powder.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.440
Understood!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.410
Hey, Jim!

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.740
Yes?

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.200
Go get some butter from the kitchen!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:45.870
Lots of it!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:46.700
Butter?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.160
That's right!
Get moving!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.620
Okay!

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.890
Here they are, Silver.
Three barrels of powder!

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.890
Silver, I have the butter!

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:11.310
Perfect. Jim, you're going to cover the barrels with butter.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.270
Top to bottom, so the water cannot pass through.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:17.850
There, that's it. Be careful to evenly coat the cracks.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.080
Alright, let them go!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.300
Now I understand!
So that's his plan...

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.360
It worked!

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.330
Silver!

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:26.780
Don't worry.
His wound opened up a little,

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.730
but it'll heal quickly.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:41.860
Aren't you glad, Silver?

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:44.100
Only three more days until you can take off those bandages.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.530
You took very good care of me, Jim.

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:48.210
Thanks a lot.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:52.090
No, it's nothing.
It's you who took care of me.

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:56.860
That was great work, Silver.

00:21:56.860 --> 00:21:59.550
Tell me, where did you learn such a maneuver?

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:03.500
Nowhere, I just followed my intuition.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.720
Just the intuition of an ordinary cook.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:09.600
An ordinary cook, huh?
Anyways, thank you.

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.000
No need, it was my pleasure.

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.010
Jim, have you forgotten your potato duty?

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:21.060
Part of your punishment hasn't been cleared!
It hasn't been a week yet!

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:23.650
Yes, sir!
On it, on it, on it!

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:32.000
To      be        continued

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.210
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.210
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.020
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.020
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:50.230
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:50.230
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:55.670
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:55.670
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.670 --> 00:23:01.080
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.670 --> 00:23:01.080
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.540
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.540
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:12.170
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:12.170
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:18.030
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:18.030
Will be brought back

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:24.620
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:24.620
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:30.510
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:30.510
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:40.230
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:40.230
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:46.230
What a surprise!

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:51.240
The investigation I lead with Silver when I learn
that Hands is planning a mutiny turns up empty,

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:54.800
but in fact, it's far worse than I thought.

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:57.480
Hidden in the barrel of apples,

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:59.880
I hear something unbelievable.

00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:01.580
I feel like I want to die!

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:04.800
Next time, the climax of the first half of Treasure Island:

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:06.880
"Heard from the Inside of an Apple Barrel!"

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.360
Can you believe it?

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.330
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.330
*

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.330
Next time

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.330
Coming soon!

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:13.330
Heard From The Inside
Of An Apple Barrel!
